  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Find the inverse of $h(x)=\\frac{3x+4}{5x-6}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p20-q15-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "h^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+4}{5x-3},\\quad x\\ne\\frac35",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{3x+4}{5x-6}\\\\x&=\\frac{3y+4}{5y-6}\\\\x(5y-6)&=3y+4\\\\5xy-6x&=3y+4\\\\(5x-3)y&=6x+4\\\\y&=\\frac{6x+4}{5x-3}\\\\h^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{6x+4}{5x-3},\\quad x\\ne\\frac35\\end{align*}$$\nThe original function has domain $x\\ne\\frac65$ and range $y\\ne\\frac35$. The inverse has domain $x\\ne\\frac35$ and range $y\\ne\\frac65$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
